  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governance for Growth (GfG) - Phase 4</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The phase 4 of GfG will build on the model of a DFAT Officer embedded in the Prime Ministers&#x2019; Office and being an adaptive and responsive mechanism to leverage opportunities for reform.  It will introduce a capacity to support medium and long term endeavours of the GoV in PFM reform and economic growth through more planned and resourced support, while continuing to utilise Direct Funding Agreements with central government agencies (MFEM, Trade and PMO). The scope of the GFG investment will incorporate engagement with the private sector and civil society through more formal recognition in EOPO3, which builds on recent efforts and partnerships.  This includes grant funding to the Chamber of Commerce, and potential grants to civil society, related to building demand for better economic governance and stimulating reform in the political economy, through activities such as research, leadership development in economic analysis, media, locally driven public events, and creating opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
